---
title: "Keycloak topology — proposed (docs/keycloak-migration-plan.md, not yet implemented). One realm 'ucms': the SPA gets a public PKCE client, each backend service gets its own confidential client_credentials client scoped to only the realm roles it needs. Every service validates tokens against Keycloak's JWKS; the Gateway has no client of its own. Existing business-to-business calls (see microservices-architecture.mmd) are omitted here for clarity — this diagram is only about the Keycloak relationship."
---
flowchart TB
    SPA["Angular SPA<br/>keycloak-js / keycloak-angular<br/>client: ucms-web (public, PKCE)"]
    KC["Keycloak<br/>realm: ucms<br/>issues + validates every token"]
    KCSCHEMA[("ucms.keycloak")]
    KC --- KCSCHEMA

    GW["API Gateway<br/>validates signature via Keycloak JWKS<br/>no client of its own"]

    IAM["Identity and Access<br/>svc-identity-access<br/>(no outbound calls → no roles needed)"]
    BASE["Base<br/>svc-base — academic:read"]
    ACAD["Academic Structure<br/>svc-academic-structure — identity:read<br/>+ AssignmentCache (Redis)"]
    ENR["Enrollment<br/>svc-enrollment — academic:read, identity:read"]
    GRADE["Assignment and Grading<br/>svc-assignment-grading — academic:read,<br/>enrollment:read, base:read, identity:read"]
    NOTIF["Notification<br/>svc-notification — identity:read, enrollment:read"]
    ANALYTICS["Analytics and Reporting<br/>svc-analytics-reporting — identity:read,<br/>academic:read, enrollment:read, assignment-grading:read"]

    SPA -->|"1. redirect: hosted login page"| KC
    KC -->|"2. authorization code"| SPA
    SPA -->|"3. exchange code for tokens"| KC
    SPA -->|"4. API calls, Bearer access_token"| GW
    GW -->|JWKS, cached| KC
    GW --> IAM
    GW --> BASE
    GW --> ACAD
    GW --> ENR
    GW --> GRADE
    GW --> NOTIF
    GW --> ANALYTICS

    CC["each service's own<br/>client_credentials grant<br/>(see keycloak-03-service-to-service.mmd)"]
    BASE -.-> CC
    ACAD -.-> CC
    ENR -.-> CC
    GRADE -.-> CC
    NOTIF -.-> CC
    ANALYTICS -.-> CC
    CC -.-> KC

    REDIS[("Redis<br/>ucms:assignments:&lt;userId&gt;")]
    ACAD <-->|cache the assignments claim| REDIS
    IAM -->|invalidate on role/scope change| REDIS

